{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine the smallest integer value of \\( b \\) such that the decimal number \\( 423_{10} \\) expressed in base \\( b \\) also has 3 digits, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the range for 3-digit numbers in base \\( b \\):**\n   A 3-digit number in base \\( b \\) ranges from \\( b^2 \\) to \\( b^3 - 1 \\). Therefore, we need:\n   \\[\n   b^2 \\leq 423 < b^3\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find the lower bound \\( b^2 \\leq 423 \\):**\n   \\[\n   b^2 \\leq 423\n   \\]\n   Taking the square root of both sides:\n   \\[\n   b \\leq \\sqrt{423}\n   \\]\n   Calculating the square root:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{423} \\approx 20.567\n   \\]\n   Since \\( b \\) must be an integer, we take the floor value:\n   \\[\n   b \\leq 20\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the upper bound \\( 423 < b^3 \\):**\n   \\[\n   423 < b^3\n   \\]\n   Taking the cube root of both sides:\n   \\[\n   b > \\sqrt[3]{423}\n   \\]\n   Calculating the cube root:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt[3]{423} \\approx 7.507\n   \\]\n   Since \\( b \\) must be an integer, we take the ceiling value:\n   \\[\n   b > 7.507 \\implies b \\geq 8\n   \\]\n\n","prefix_end":1002,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,279,24632,7546,897,315,17767,293,1124,8,1741,429,279,12122,1372,17767,220,19,17,18,15159,16,15,92,1124,8,13302,304,2331,17767,293,1124,8,1083,702,220,18,18509,11,582,1184,311,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,16250,2685,279,2088,369,220,18,48342,5109,304,2331,17767,293,1124,1648,1019,256,362,220,18,48342,1372,304,2331,17767,293,1124,8,21283,504,17767,293,61,17,1124,8,311,17767,293,61,18,481,220,16,1124,568,15277,11,582,1184,510,256,1124,9640,256,293,61,17,1124,273,80,220,19,17,18,366,293,61,18,198,256,1124,2533,17,13,3070,9885,279,4722,6822,17767,293,61,17,1124,273,80,220,19,17,18,1124,1648,1019,256,1124,9640,256,293,61,17,1124,273,80,220,19,17,18,198,256,1124,921,256,35825,2