45,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,3838,374,279,24632,7546,897,315,400,65,3,1741,429,400,19,17,18,15159,16,15,31716,13302,304,2331,400,65,3,1083,702,400,18,3,18509,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the smallest integer value of $b$ such that $423_{10}$ expressed in base $b$ also has $3$ digits?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"31f275e1e4f8aa7dc78566c2586547aab03e82f02935c104e7af0d470ec80456"},"seconds":16.211570262908936,"seed":300262255657881355,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine the smallest integer value of \\( b \\) such that the decimal number \\( 423_{10} \\) expressed in base \\( b \\) also has 3 digits, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the range for 3-digit numbers in base \\( b \\):**\n   A 3-digit number in base \\( b \\) ranges from \\( b^2 \\) to \\( b^3 - 1 \\). Therefore, we need:\n   \\[\n   b^2 \\leq 423 < b^3\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find the lower bound \\( b^2 \\leq 423 \\):**\n   \\[\n   b^2 \\leq 423\n   \\]\n   Taking the square root of both sides:\n   \\[\n   b \\leq \\sqrt{423}\n   \\]\n   Calculating the square root:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{423} \\approx 20.567\n   \\]\n   Since \\( b \\) must be an integer, we take the floor value:\n   \\[\n   b \\leq 20\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the upper bound \\( 423 < b^3 \\):**\n   \\[\n   423 < b^3\n   \\]\n   Taking the cube root of both sides:\n   \\[\n   b > \\sqrt[3]{423}\n   \\]\n   Calculating the cube root:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt[3]{423} \\approx 7.507\n   \\]\n   Since \\( b \\) must be an integer, we take the ceiling value:\n   \\[\n   b > 7.507 \\implies b \\geq 8\n   \\]\n\n4. **Combine the bounds:**\n   From the above calculations, we have:\n   \\[\n   8 \\leq b \\leq 20\n   \\]\n   The smallest integer value of \\( b \\) that satisfies both conditions is \\( b = 8 \\).\n\n5. **Verify the solution:**\n   Convert \\( 423_{10} \\) to base 8 to ensure it is a 3-digit number.\n   \\[\n   423 \\div 8 = 52 \\text{ remainder } 7\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   52 \\div 8 = 6 \\text{ remainder } 4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   6 \\div 8 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 6\n   \\]\n   Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get:\n   \\[\n   423_{10} = 647_8\n   \\]\n   This is indeed a 3-digit number in base 8.\n\nTherefore, the smallest integer value of \\( b \\) such that \\( 423_{10} \\) expressed in base \\( b \\) has 3 digits is \\(\\boxed{8}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{8}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:406"}
